description: Three places where a program that runs natively has no twin on either lane, found during the pin-move row run (git-issue:a7ee80a) and covered by no row:
 
 - Long/parseLong has no twin.
 - Integer/parseInt takes no radix argument.
 - NumberFormatException is not a catch class, so (try (Integer/parseInt "x") (catch NumberFormatException e ...)) cannot be written for both lanes.
 
 Facts that close it: F1, each of the three runs on both lanes with the native result, witnessed by a case per item in corpus/wasm/review-shapes.lg with its expected output; F2, a program catching NumberFormatException around a bad parse prints the same on native and on each lane.
